# ============================================================================
# 1. PRIVACY - AUDIO AND TRANSCRIPTS. READ THIS BEFORE FORCE-ADDING ANYTHING.
# ============================================================================
# Overlayy captures microphone and system audio from live calls. Any recording
# in this repo may contain other people's voices, and once pushed to a public
# remote it is permanent - a force-push does not remove it from forks, clones,
# or GitHub's cached views.
#
# These rules are deliberately broad. If a test needs audio:
#   - PREFER generating a synthetic tone in test code (no binary in git), or
#   - fetch a public dataset via a script into fixtures/audio/ (gitignored), or
#   - as a last resort, `git add -f` a file you are CERTAIN contains no real
#     human speech, and say why in the commit message.
#
# Never `git add -f` anything matching this section without re-listening to it.

# raw and encoded audio
*.wav
*.wave
*.aif
*.aiff
*.aifc
*.caf
*.pcm
*.raw
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.mp4
*.aac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.flac
*.wma
*.amr

# capture-harness output (C3 dump-to-WAV) and VAD fixtures (C4)
recordings/
fixtures/audio/
audio/
captures/
*.dump

# transcripts and transcript-adjacent data - derived from real speech
*.vtt
*.srt
*.sbv
*.dfxp
transcripts/
*.transcript.*
*.srt.json

# session dumps, prompt/response payloads, and latency telemetry (F0 section 12)
# can all contain verbatim conversation content
sessions/
telemetry/
*.jsonl
*.ndjson
*.har

# local LLM/STT provider caches and request recordings
.cache/
.recordings/
*.betamax

# --- the ONE exception -----------------------------------------------------
# Synthetic fixtures only: generated tones, hand-written fake transcripts that
# were never spoken by anyone, constructed conversation windows for B4.
# The path name is the safeguard - if you are about to put something here, the
# word "synthetic" should make you stop and check.
#
# Better still: build fixtures in test code (Python dicts, Swift structs) rather
# than as data files. Then there is nothing to leak and nothing to police.
#
# Anything real - a recording, a real transcript, a real session dump - has no
# exception and no path into this repo.
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/**


