# ============================================================================
# 6. PRIVATE WORKING AREA - the only docs path that is ignored
# ============================================================================
# Use this for anything you would not want on a public remote: product
# strategy, competitor notes, personal retros, half-formed ideas.
# Everything else under docs/ IS committed and MUST stay committed -
# docs/DECISIONS.md is append-only precisely so git history preserves it.
docs/internal/


# ============================================================================
# DELIBERATELY *NOT* IGNORED - do not add these
# ============================================================================
#   AGENTS.md                      agent entry point; must be versioned
#   docs/STATUS.md                 living state; fresh sessions depend on it
#   docs/DECISIONS.md              append-only log; history IS the artifact
#   docs/F0_PROTOCOL.md            versioned contract with a changelog
#   docs/LEARNINGS.md              learning log; prediction accuracy needs history
#   docs/components/*-BRIEF.md     pre-design predictions; the learning baseline
#   .opencode/                     tutor/reviewer agents and commands are part
#                                  of the system, not personal tool config
#   overlayy_roadmap*.md           design rationale referenced by DECISIONS
#   overlayy.png                   UI mock referenced by D-011
#   Package.resolved               Swift dependency lockfile - commit it
#   uv.lock / requirements.txt     Python dependency lockfiles - commit them
#   .python-version                pins the 3.12 runtime
#   .github/                       PR template and CI workflows
